<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43707" root="&#xA;                        ملك&#xA;                    " body-key="m1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِلِيك</span></b> 
                         is also <i>syn. with</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَمْلُوكٌ</span>; this is meant
in the TA where it is said that <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُلَكَآءُ</span> in the saying <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَبَا مُلُوكٌ وَلَيْسَ لَبَا مُلَكَآءُ</span> [<i>We have kings</i> of
bees, <i>but we have not slaves</i>] is pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَلِيكُ</span>
from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المَمْلُوكُ</span>: it is also said in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رغو</span> in the
TA, (see 4 in that art.) that <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَلِيكَةٌ</span> is syn. with
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَمْلُوكَةٌ</span>.

  </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
